From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 31/31] cuda/hip: GDN conv-chain fold - concat + conv + silu + state writeback in one kernel (+2.7% decode)

Round-12 profiling put numbers on the wall-vs-kernel gap: decode runs
~1085 kernels/token (6.1ms busy) inside a 7.8ms token - ~1.5us of
replay/dispatch overhead per node (hipGraphLaunch alone is ~500us of CPU
per token, submission scaling with node count). Node-count reduction is
therefore worth ~1.5us/node on top of any kernel time saved.

Every GDN layer runs a three-kernel conv chain per decode token:
CONCAT(state_window, x_t) materializes a [4, 8192] window (1.77us),
SSM_CONV(+fused SILU) convolves it (1.58us), and a CPY writes the shifted
window back to the conv cache (2.03us). All three collapse into one
1.6us kernel: each thread owns a channel, reads the 3-value state window
and x_t into registers (making the in-place cache writeback alias-safe by
construction), computes the conv with the stock loop structure, applies
silu, and stores the shifted window. 60 launches and ~92us of kernel time
per token disappear.

Detection (eval-loop, done-set pattern like the grouped launches): a
dim-0 F32 CONCAT of [3, nr] with [1, nr] whose only consumers in the
layer window are one SSM_CONV and one CPY of the concat tail view
(positions 1..3) onto a contiguous f32 cache view. View/metadata nodes
over the concat are skipped; any other consumer declines. n_t == 1 only
(prefill keeps stock nodes), d_conv == 4, no conv bias, single writeback
(rollback-snapshot graphs decline via the extra CPY consumers).
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_SSM_CONV_FOLD=1 restores stock.

Measured (runner box, same-binary toggle, 30-patch base):

- decode trace: concat_cont, fused ssm_conv_f32 and the conv writeback
  cpy_scalar (990 dispatches each) all replaced by 990x ssm_conv_fold_f32
  (1.60us); total decode kernel 201.9 -> 198.9ms per 33 tokens
- tg128 toggle A/B, 5 rounds: 127.68-128.11 -> 131.33-131.41 tok/s
  (+2.7%, 5/5 rounds separated, arms fully disjoint)
- pp512: neutral (4239-4266 off vs 4204-4259 on, overlapping; the fold
  cannot fire at prefill by the n_t gate)
- ppl (runner corpus, 3 loads): 3.9271/3.9283/3.9256 vs stock 3.9314
  (-0.08..-0.15%, band 0.5%)
- test-backend-ops SSM_CONV and CONCAT suites OK (fold does not touch
  the generic ops); concurrent 8-request greedy smoke coherent
- greedy identity, fold on vs off (same binary): short/math prompts
  byte-exact; mid/code/long drift mid-completion at 53-77% common
  prefixes. Both arms are individually run-to-run DETERMINISTIC
  (A/A byte-exact on every prompt); the fused kernel's accumulation
  contracts differently than the stock three-kernel chain (same
  expression, different codegen context) - the same ppl-gated
  reassociation class as 0024/0026/0028, disclosed and verified on
  this track three times.
---
